{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Turned a prose claim in the knowledge index into a citable one. The entry that states the incumbent answered neither the pre-vote nor the vote request already named the receipt it came from, and that same receipt contains the two events that witness it, so I added indices 12 and 16 of CheckRun 4ff9bf25cb164dd8bcf9d3be02aa1568 — q_prevote_at_incumbent and q_vote_at_incumbent, each recording node 1 with responded false — to the entry's executions. I verified both indices against the receipt before citing them; they are exactly the two events the sentence describes, so the claim that the lease suppressed both requests now rests on recorded witnesses rather than on the wording of the entry. The statement, conditions and sources are unchanged, and the only changed field is executions, which keeps the update honest about what moved. This also closes a small gap that the correction earlier this run made visible: I had learned to distrust a bare responded flag, and here the same pair of flags is the evidence for the opposite conclusion, which is only sound because the entry's claim is about the absence of a response and the flags record exactly that. Nothing else was touched, submission validates with execution_requested=false, and the record still has no uncited executions.\"}"}}
